# constructs — which can leave neither by being fixed nor by being triaged
# — were counted inside a number captioned "ratchet toward 0", and a real
# wrong answer could enter behind a frontier refusal that left. Ceilings
# are now per class in baselines/untriaged-count; raising `wrong-answer`
# above 0 requires an explicit reviewable two-file edit (a row here + the
# ceiling there, justified in the same commit), independent of frontier
# churn. An id here with no valid
# disposition, or a current unexplained id with no row here at all, FAILS
# the gate — the classification is never optional.
